# Publication allow-list enforcement.
# These are internal development docs / an early prototype that must NOT ship in
# the public release. `git archive` (the supported way to build the publication
# tree) honors `export-ignore` and drops them automatically — so the exclusion is
# enforced by the repo, not by a manual step. Build the release tree with:
#     git archive --format=tar HEAD | tar -x -C <dest>
# then run `git ls-files` on <dest> and confirm none of the below appear.
HANDOFF.md      export-ignore
ARCHITECTURE.md export-ignore
DESIGN_UX.md    export-ignore
prototype/      export-ignore
